      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not explicitly define an “informant” as “another person who gives a report … rather than the adult reporting on themselves”; it only states that a measure uses both “self-report and an informant report.”",
        "The specific framing that the informant report is “used alongside the self-report to describe everyday executive functioning” is only indirectly supported; the packet mentions executive functions “in their everyday environment” and that both report types are used, but it does not explicitly connect the informant report to “everyday executive functioning” in that exact way."
